## Structs Own Their Fields

A struct owns everything inside it. Moving the struct moves all fields:

```xiom
type Person = { name: Str; age: Int; }

fn process(p: Person) {
  io.println(p.name);
  // p is dropped here — name and age cleaned up
}

fn main() -> Int {
  let alice = Person{ name: "Alice", age: 30 };
  process(alice);       // Ownership of entire Person moves
  // io.println(alice.name);  // ERROR: alice was moved!
  return 0;
}
```

### Borrowing Struct Fields

```xiom
fn read_name(p: &Person) {
  io.println(p.name);  // Reading a field through a borrow
}

fn birthday(p: &mut Person) {
  p.age = p.age + 1;   // Modifying a field through &mut
}

fn main() -> Int {
  var person = Person{ name: "Bob", age: 25 };
  read_name(&person);
  birthday(&mut person);
  return person.age;
}
```

### Partial Moves

```xiom
type Pair = { first: Str; second: Str; }

fn main() -> Int {
  let pair = Pair{ first: "hello", second: "world" };
  let f = pair.first;  // Moves just 'first' out
  // io.println(pair.first);  // ERROR: first was moved
  io.println(pair.second);    // OK — second wasn't moved
  return pair.second.len() as Int;
}
```

